    <string name="app_name">LipaBill</string>
    <!-- Keep in sync with AccessibilityServiceDisclosure (system Settings screen only). -->
    <string name="accessibility_service_description">
        LipaBill uses Android’s AccessibilityService API to help complete M-Pesa USSD payments
        you start and confirm in the app (Send money, Pay bill/till/Pochi, and Repeat).
        After you confirm and enter your PIN on LipaBill’s secure keypad, the service may read
        on-screen USSD prompts and fill the next step for that payment session only.
        That on-screen text is not stored as a transcript, not sent off this phone, and not shared.
        It does not read SMS, does not change system settings, and is not used to control
        unrelated apps when you are not paying. Your M-Pesa PIN is never stored.
        You can turn this service off anytime in Android Accessibility settings.
    </string>
